# Security Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines define core security practices for protecting user data and application integrity. All team members must adhere to these principles with no exceptions.

## Best Practices
- Never store sensitive data (passwords, tokens) in plain text
- Implement proper authentication and authorization flows
- Use secure communication channels (HTTPS, TLS)
- Apply the principle of least privilege
- Sanitize all user inputs to prevent injection attacks
- Implement proper session management
- Use platform-specific secure storage for sensitive data
- Keep dependencies updated to avoid known vulnerabilities
- Remove debug logs in production
- Implement certificate pinning for high-security features

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize security-related code in dedicated files/directories
- Use `.env` files (excluded from git) for environment-specific secrets
- Implement security services in `lib/core/security/`
- Structure:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      security/
        encryption_service.dart
        secure_storage.dart
        auth_utils.dart
      constants/
        api_endpoints.dart (no secrets)
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use named constructors for secure object creation
- Implement secure disposal methods for sensitive data
- Mark sensitive fields as `@protected` or private
- Use strong typing for security-critical parameters
- Avoid security-related string literals in code
- Implement toString() methods that hide sensitive data
- Document security assumptions and requirements

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Use appropriate encryption strength (balance security vs performance)
- Cache authentication state carefully
- Implement lazy loading for security services
- Avoid blocking the main thread with crypto operations
- Balance security measures against performance requirements
- Consider using platform channels for critical security operations
- Benchmark security operations to identify bottlenecks

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test authentication flows comprehensively
- Implement security-focused integration tests
- Verify secure storage implementations
- Test token refresh and session expiration
- Validate input sanitization functions
- Test offline security measures
- Verify proper cleanup of sensitive data
- Conduct regular security code reviews
- Implement penetration testing for critical features
